      "category": "engine",
      "title": "3.1L/3.4L V6 Intake Manifold Gasket Leak (Dex-Cool)",
      "description": "The 3.1L and 3.4L pushrod V6 engines in the Lumina develop intake manifold gasket leaks, often attributed to Dex-Cool coolant reacting with the composite gaskets. Coolant leaks externally and can also enter the crankcase.",
      "solution": "Pressure-test the cooling system and inspect around the lower intake manifold for external seepage; if coolant is disappearing or the oil is contaminated, remove the upper and lower intake manifold and confirm gasket failure. Repair is to replace the lower intake manifold gaskets with the updated metal/rubber design, install revised intake bolts if specified, change the engine oil and filter, thoroughly flush the Dex-Cool-contaminated cooling system, and refill/bleed with the correct coolant mix while checking for bearing damage if coolant entered the crankcase. Parts typically run about $80-$200, but labor is substantial at roughly 6-10 hours, so total repair cost is commonly $700-$1,500 depending on shop rates and whether related items like coolant elbows, thermostat, or pushrods are replaced at the same time.",
      "severity": "high",
      "confidence": "medium",
      "symptoms": [
        "Coolant loss",
        "Oil milkshake under oil cap",
        "Overheating",
        "Sweet coolant smell",
        "Low coolant light"
      ],
      "affectedSystems": [],
      "dtcCodes": [
        "P0171",
        "P0174"
      ],
